# How to cite this software. Read by GitHub (the "Cite this repository" button) and by
# Zenodo, so a reader does not have to guess at a citation and get it wrong.
#
# This file exists because a prior review named its absence as a reviewer's first
# question: "How do I cite this software, and who are the authors with their ORCIDs and
# affiliations?" It had no answer anywhere in the project.
#
# NO ORCID FIELD. Taylor's is not recorded here yet, and an invented or guessed identifier
# is worse than a missing one — it resolves to a real person who is not the author. Add it
# under `authors:` when you have it, as `orcid: "https://orcid.org/<your-id>"`.
#
# The example is written that way on purpose: a literal placeholder id in this comment
# tripped the very test that forbids shipping one, which is the test working.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: runprov
abstract: >-
  Records what a script read, wrote and ran as, in a form a checker can verify. Inputs are
  hashed at the moment they are opened, the resulting pin is written into the artifact
  itself rather than only into a sidecar, and the pin is deterministic so that a changed
  header means changed inputs. Zero runtime dependencies.
version: 0.2.0
# NO `date-released` YET, and that is a statement rather than an omission: this version has
# not been released. Zenodo and GitHub render a citation without a year until it is set, and
# a citation without a year is a poor one -- so `python ci.py release-check` (which `build`
# runs, and which ships beside this file) refuses a release whose CHANGELOG says released
# while this field is missing, and refuses a version TAG whose CHANGELOG section still reads
# `[Unreleased]`. Set it to the tag date, YYYY-MM-DD. Inventing a date for an unreleased
# package would be the same class of error as the placeholder ORCID this file already
# refuses.
license: CECILL-B
repository-code: "https://github.com/Taylor-Nicole/runprov"
keywords:
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - data lineage
authors:
  - family-names: Thompson
    given-names: Taylor
    affiliation: "AP-HP, Hôpital Henri-Mondor, Créteil, France"
